lood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued November 1 at 7:09PM MST until November 6 at 1:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The Flood Watch continues for the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa Vicinity/Central San Luis\nValley.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...flooding is forecasted to\nbegin by mid week.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is forecasted\nto begin by mid week.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday morning to late Thursday night.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:30 PM MST Sunday the stage was 3.0 feet.\n- Forecast...Flood stage may be reached late Wednesday morning.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-06T01:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a3cd340f9b1b099614785410803556c44c7ca26c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a3cd340f9b1b099614785410803556c44c7ca26c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued November 1 at 1:50PM MST until November 4 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will be possible,\nespecially over the western half of San Luis Valley.\n\n* WHERE...The western half of the San Luis Valley, including\nAntonito, Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM MST this afternoon through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, in